pptx-edit is authored by the ultrawork project (not derived from Anthropic's proprietary
document skills). It is licensed under the same terms as the ultrawork repository.

It was named `doc-edit` until 2026-08-04 and also carried thin .docx/.xlsx read/edit
scripts; those were dropped once the dedicated `docx` and `xlsx` skills superseded them
(discussions/059 S6), leaving in-place .pptx editing — which nothing else covers.

It invokes the following third-party Python library at runtime (NOT bundled; installed by
the user per the SKILL.md instructions):
  - python-pptx (MIT)
